    "humanReview": "Qualitative user approval; numeric ratings remain unmeasured.",
    "entrance": "West balcony above the paired pod and seed.",
    "exit": "High eastern balcony beyond the second pod.",
    "solution": "Walk off the west balcony. Cut diagonally down-right with Jump released: the same blade contact makes a low pod rebound and knocks the adjacent impulse seed down-right. Drift past the moved seed while its charge finishes, then face down-left and cut its gold face during the descent. The seed launches up-right toward the distant pod pair. Hold Jump on the next downward cut to loft onto the high exit, preserving the seed's lateral speed.",
    "nearestExisting": "B32 chooses low and lofted rebounds around a portal, while F36 relocates an impulse before a separate return climb. Here the first low rebound is also the physical preparation of the later seed launch; the return interception occurs during that rebound, and its sideways speed carries through the final loft.",
    "novelty": "One diagonal blade stroke prepares two different objects at once. The knight goes up while the seed goes down, then the same arc brings them together in a new relative position. Low versus lofted rebound is selected twice for opposite purposes.",
    "designNotes": "Zero dashes makes the seed the necessary lateral bridge. First roof rejects loft, lower thorns reject walking into an easy seed setup, and the exit face denies a climb shortcut. No secret exit-event condition. The starting pod and seed are adjacent and separately visible. Their double-contact window spans ten approach timings (32\u201341 frames), each producing both low rebound and seed preparation. Different early cuts change the later interception; the player still aims at the moved seed. The far two-pod cluster widens the landing contact.",
